{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d3a6c1f2-8b47-4e05-9a1c-2f7e5b9d0c41",
    "name": "ServiceNow Direct - Bag Registration & Counting Results",
    "description": "Calls ServiceNow's bag_registration and counting_results endpoints DIRECTLY, bypassing our own DK API. Internal testing only - not partner-facing.\n\nAuth: HTTP Basic, user BizTalkIntegration. Fill snUsername/snPassword from Key Vault kv-dev-nokasapi-cashmgmt, secret ServiceNow--Dk--Credential (JSON with baseUrl/username/password). Never commit real values into this file.\n\nRegistration creates records in the ServiceNow DEV instance. Set nokasClientId to a client id ServiceNow has registered as a source (an unregistered one returns HTTP 500 'Unknown source').\n\nNotes (2026-09-25): counting_results moved to /counting_results/dk and its startDate/endDate now filter on LAST-MODIFIED time, given as 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss' in ServiceNow's own Central European time (NOT UTC - a bag registered 06:14 UTC reads 08:14 there). Rows carry clientID, registered date and count date. Bag labels must be issued to the customer's account (for kardex 4200000198 the label starts with 4200198).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
