  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Bag Registration (POST bag_registration)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 Register bag - valid, with nokasSource (expect 200 success)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{snBaseUrl}}/bag_registration",
              "host": [
                "{{snBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "bag_registration"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bagRegistration\": {\n    \"customerRefNumber\": \"{{customerRefNumber}}\",\n    \"cashRegisterId\": \"POS-01\",\n    \"messageId\": \"{{messageId}}\",\n    \"bagNumber\": \"{{bagNumber}}\",\n    \"registrationDate\": \"{{registrationDate}}\",\n    \"totalOrderAmount\": \"700.00\",\n    \"bagItemsLC\": {\n      \"DKK_500\": \"1\",\n      \"DKK_200\": \"1\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"nokasSource\": {\n    \"customerId\": \"{{nokasClientId}}\",\n    \"customerName\": \"{{nokasCustomerName}}\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "description": "Exactly what our API sends: the partner's bagRegistration object plus nokasSource. bagNumber must be a label issued to the customer's account (for kardex 4200000198 it starts with 4200198); otherwise ServiceNow answers HTTP 500 {result:{status:'failed', message:'The bag label number must belong to the account...'}}. A success creates a record in the ServiceNow TEST instance - the reply message names it (NOC...), saved to {{lastRecordNumber}}. Success shape: { result: { status: 'success', message: '...NOC... was created.' } } (the id field has appeared as sys_id and as message_id). Requires {{nokasClientId}} to be a registered source."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('bagNumber', '4200198' + String(Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) % 100000).padStart(5, '0'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('messageId', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('registrationDate', new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const r = pm.response.json().result || {};",
                  "pm.test('status is success', () => pm.expect(r.status).to.eql('success'));",
                  "const m = /(NOC\\d+)/.exec(r.message || '');",
                  "if (m) { pm.collectionVariables.set('lastRecordNumber', m[1]); console.log('Created', m[1]); }",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastBagNumber', pm.collectionVariables.get('bagNumber'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
